<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Italian Social Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1943 CE – 1945 CE · capital Salo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Fascist puppet state set up by Nazi Germany in northern Italy in 1943, with Mussolini at its head, which collapsed in April 1945.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> signed an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> in September 1943, German forces occupied northern and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. German paratroopers freed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a> from captivity on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gran-sasso">Gran Sasso</a>, and he proclaimed a new Fascist state, with ministries scattered around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-garda">Lake Garda</a>, especially at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salo">Salò</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic depended entirely on German forces, who controlled the economy and deported Italian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> and workers. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verona-manifesto">Verona Manifesto</a> of 1943 promised a socialist-style programme, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-verona">Verona</a> trial of January 1944 executed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galeazzo-ciano">Galeazzo Ciano</a> and others who had voted against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a>. Its militias and the Germans waged a bitter war against the partisan resistance, with reprisals against civilians.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Allied offensive and a general partisan uprising in April 1945 brought collapse. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a> was captured while fleeing towards <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/swiss-confederation">Switzerland</a> and shot on 28 April 1945, and the German forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> surrendered on 2 May.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/italian-social-republic.jpg" alt="Italian Social Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: See below. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Italy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1943 CE – 1945 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Salo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Benito Mussolini</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Salo, Repubblica Sociale Italiana</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1944&amp;focus=italian-social-republic" aria-label="Italian Social Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4930 570 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Italian Social Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5250 826L5304 942M5250 826L5300 622M5250 826L5197 811"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0M5300 622h0M5197 811h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5250 826h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5250 826h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Salo. <a href="/atlas?year=1944&amp;focus=italian-social-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
